{"type":"done","text":"The workbook is built, and every one of the 18 requirements has at least one test case (no uncovered ones reported).\n\n- **Files:** in `output/2026-11-19-c47bf2/`: `leave-management-system-v2_TestCases.xlsx`, the source JSON, and three TestRail CSVs (`_testrail_functional.csv`, `_testrail_api.csv`, `_testrail_roles.csv`).\n- **Counts:** 124 cases: 81 functional, 26 API (FR-5 lists three endpoints) and 17 role-based, plus a permission matrix for Employee, Manager and HR Admin. By type: 26 positive, 39 negative, 27 corner, 32 boundary. By priority: 64 High, 41 Medium, 19 Low. That's 52% High, above the 25–40% guideline, because of the many security and permission-denial cases. You may want to move some to Medium.\n- **Top open questions:** are leave days counted as calendar or working days? Is Annual balance taken on submission or on approval, and do pending requests count against it? Which timezone decides that a start date is \"in the past\"? Do failed logins during a lock extend it? What can HR Admin approve, and who approves leave for managers and HR Admins? The workbook also lists 11 assumptions and 13 open questions in total.\n- **TestRail import:** go to Test Cases → Import → CSV, choose the \"Test Case (Text)\" template, and map the columns. The Section column (`Module > Category`) can be mapped to a section hierarchy.","t":1795076332771}
